Subject: [PATCH] Backport native IPv4 link-local fallback to 1.43.7-dev

Base: NetworkManager upstream tag 1.43.7-dev
Base-commit: 2e3fabae50be1429e451c85f32ef9b7011b8feae
Upstream-Status: Backport

Combine the upstream IPv4LL fallback feature with the address tracking and
lease-loss handling it depends on. No external avahi-autoipd is needed.
Existing default/auto/disabled/enabled link-local settings retain their
meaning. The new fallback value is 4.

Upstream commits (Dominique Martinet and Beniamino Galvani):
  a80fef9f37c890947f9d4f90965341a1d6cc8516
    dhcp: remove l3cds when the lease expires
  b39e38f272e8d60b2c908aba4c1f19ce055c57ba
    device: set dhcpx state back to pending when lease lost
  b3d2902ad4339f183d1316f305292062b087a358
    l3cfg: add new NM_L3_CONFIG_DAT_FLAGS_HAS_IPV4_NON_LL flag
  c575293f1b08d742e53282a1c2cc1b5cc567436f
    device: add ipv4.link-local=fallback (IPv4LL set iff no other IPv4 set)
  abbaa9b62906fbfe87c730eb83476285cb1f18e1
    libnm, nmcli: fix "Since" version for ipv4.link-local=fallback

Commit URLs use:
  https://github.com/NetworkManager/NetworkManager/commit/<full-hash>

Backport adaptations:
  - Adapt NEWS and the older nmcli metadata description format.
  - Add a focused settings-verification regression test.
  - Runtime changes are taken from the upstream commits above.

Apply in your NetworkManager source tree:
  git apply --check /path/to/0001-nm-1.43.7-native-ipv4ll-fallback.patch
  git apply /path/to/0001-nm-1.43.7-native-ipv4ll-fallback.patch

Rebuild and deploy NetworkManager, libnm and nmcli together using the target
image's existing build recipe. This patch is checked against the upstream
base, not against an unavailable vendor-modified source tree.

After disabling the Avahi udev/service integration and stopping existing
avahi-autoipd processes, configure and reactivate the intended NM profile:
  nmcli connection modify "<profile>" ipv4.method auto ipv4.link-local fallback
Reactivation interrupts connectivity; arrange local access first.

Fallback is based on configured addresses, not Internet reachability or
DHCP-server reachability. It can supply IPv4LL while DHCP is still pending.
A still-valid DHCP address suppresses IPv4LL. Manually configured non-LL
addresses suppress it as well.

Validation completed:
  - git diff --check
  - git apply --cached --check against the pristine upstream base
Not completed: Linux compilation, regression test execution, target tests.
The development host is macOS and has no Linux container runtime available.

Required target validation before production:
  - Run /core/general/test_setting_ip4_link_local_fallback in test-general.
  - No DHCP: obtain 169.254/16 and keep DHCP attempting acquisition.
  - DHCP becomes available: install DHCP address and withdraw IPv4LL.
  - DHCP lease expires/is NAKed: remove stale lease config and regain IPv4LL.
  - DHCP reacquisition, including the same address: IPv4LL withdraws again.
  - Cable unplug/replug and connection down/up: no stale address or LL state.
  - Static IPv4 present: no fallback LL; IPv4 disabled: no LL.
  - Existing link-local=enabled behavior still allows simultaneous addresses.
  - Reapply changes between enabled, fallback and disabled.

